cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ANet Drone4D in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "ANet Drone4D: A Real-World Grounded 4D World Runtime for Autonomous Multi-Agent Drones"
abstract: >-
  ANet Drone4D is a real-world grounded digital twin and multi-agent simulation
  platform for drones. It follows one chain, Reality to Reconstruction to World
  to Environment to Simulation to Agent: captured or reconstructed point clouds
  become versioned World Packages with geometry queries, an environment field
  adds wind, turbulence and visibility, a vectorised fleet simulator steps 1 to
  1,000 drones on one shared 250 Hz clock (real time at 1,000 drones on 0.53
  CPU core of an 8-vCPU Xeon E5-2603 v4 machine, median of 3 runs), and the
  Interactive Sandbox gives each visitor an isolated simulation core while the
  browser renders the world; its server needs no GPU. Drones are the first kind
  of physical agent; they discover each other's capabilities and delegate tasks
  through an in-process mock of the ANet network.
